From 04781aba03425673e651e7e5194c51d5d8c2b975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:35:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 44/58] topk: determinism toggles for greedy repeatability

- MERLIN_FULL_K: deterministic Marlin MoE split-K (after unmerged upstream #46639).
- MERLIN_QSA_SORT: canonical order for the QSA selected blocks.
- MERLIN_TIE_DET: deterministic tie-break at the persistent_topk cutoff.
- MERLIN_TIE_RECENT: cutoff ties keep the highest indices.
- Decode candidate truncation is detected; one tie direction across the
  medium path; the kernel switches are registered.
